  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Trailing after Texas took the lead in the first, they answered twice with runners in scoring position. That was the ceiling on their comeback chances.",
    "what_this_means": "Osleivis Basabe tied it with a home run in the seventh, but tying isn't winning. The lineup left twelve runners on base across nine innings, converting just two of them into runs. They scored in the seventh when Basabe delivered the homer, then again in the ninth when the game was already slipping away. Two critical missed opportunities. Four runners left in the second alone, another two stranded in the third. Decided this before the final pitch. The bullpen wasn't the problem. Five pitchers covered 2.2 innings of relief with no clean exit, but by then the damage was structural. This team doesn't lose because the arms fail. It loses when the bats show up but don't show out.",
    "what_to_watch": "Cody Bradford takes the ball for Texas tonight at 11:35 AM. Carson Whisenhunt goes for the Giants in what shapes as a tight matchup. These teams understand each other now, and one clean inning might be the difference.",
